.TH PSGetLayerByIndex 3 2024-03-09 "PsyC 0.9.5" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
\fBPSGetLayerByIndex\fR

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/psyc.h>

.I
PSLayer  *
.br
\fBPSGetLayerByIndex\fR(\fIPSModel *model\fR, \fIint layer_index\fR, \fIint model_index\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Get the layer at index \fIlayer_index\fR in \fImodel\fR. If \fImodel\fR is part of a multi-model chain, the argument \fImodel_index\fR can be used to specify the index of the sub-model of the model chain.
.br
Both \fIlayer_index\fR and \fImodel_index\fR accept negative values: in this case, the index is calculated from the last layer/model, for example:
.br
if \fIlayer_index\fR is -1 and \fImodel\fR has 5 layers, the actual index will be the last layer's index (4).  

.SH RETURN VALUES
The layer at specified index/indices or \fINULL\fR if:

.RS 4
\[bu] \fImodel\fR is \fINULL\fR.
.br

\[bu] \fImodel\fR is a multi-model chain but it's broken/invalid.
.br

\[bu] \fIlayer_index\fR is out-of-bounds.
.br

\[bu] \fImodel_index\fR is out-of-bounds.
.br
.RE

.SH SEE ALSO
psyc(1)
